```hcl
# modules/web-app/main.tf
variable "instance_count" {}
variable "instance_type"  {}

resource "aws_instance" "app" {
  count         = var.instance_count
  instance_type = var.instance_type
}
```
```hcl
# envs/prod/main.tf
module "app" {
  source         = "../../modules/web-app"
  instance_count = 5
  instance_type  = "m5.large"
}
```

The module's logic (what an "app" deployment looks like) is written once; `envs/dev/main.tf` calls the same module with `instance_count = 1` and a smaller type — no duplicated resource logic between environments, only duplicated (small) input values.
